## SHOULD Requirements (Strong Recommendations)

### Design Patterns

- [ ] **SHOULD NOT**: Use if/else or switch for type comparison when logic is complex
  - ❌ Poor Design: `if (type == "A") ... else if (type == "B") ... else if (type == "C")`
  - ✅ Better: Strategy Pattern, Factory Pattern, Polymorphism
  - 💡 **Acceptable if/else usage**:
    - Simple boolean conditions (`if (isEnabled)`)
    - 2-3 branches with trivial logic (<5 lines per branch)
    - One-time validation checks
    - Early returns for guard clauses
  - 🎯 **Consider refactoring when**:
    - 4+ branches in if/else chain
    - Each branch >10 lines
    - Same pattern repeated across multiple methods
    - Type checking (instanceof, typeof comparisons)

### Code Organization

- [ ] **SHOULD**: Extract methods when logic exceeds 20 lines
  - 💡 Guideline: Aim for methods ≤ 15 lines
  - 💡 Acceptable: Up to 25 lines if highly cohesive

- [ ] **SHOULD**: Split large classes into smaller components
  - 💡 Guideline: Aim for ≤ 150 lines per class
  - 💡 Trigger: When class has 5+ unrelated methods

---

## MUST NOT Requirements (Strict Prohibitions)

- [ ] **MUST NOT**: Generate code without explicit user instruction
  - ❌ Prohibited: "I also added X for convenience"
  - ✅ Allowed: "Should I also add X?"

- [ ] **MUST NOT**: Introduce >3 new concepts per iteration (unless explicitly instructed)
  - 📏 Count: New classes, interfaces, patterns combined
  - ❌ Violation: Adding 5 new classes **without user requesting it**
  - ✅ Pass: Adding 2 new classes, then confirming before more
  - 💡 **Exception**: User explicitly requests specific number
    - ✅ Allowed: "Split this file into 5 classes" → Create all 5
    - ✅ Allowed: "Refactor using Strategy pattern" → Create all required classes
    - ❌ Prohibited: User asks to "improve code" → AI adds 5 classes unprompted

- [ ] **MUST NOT**: Auto-generate ideas without approval
  - ❌ Prohibited: Unsolicited refactoring suggestions
  - ✅ Allowed: "I noticed X. Would you like me to improve it?"

---

## Quantified Standards Summary

| Metric | Limit | Tolerance | Blocking |
|--------|-------|-----------|----------|
| File length | ≤ 200 lines | 210 lines | 250+ lines |
| Method params | ≤ 3 | 4 (if justified) | 5+ params |
| Method length | ≤ 20 lines | 25 lines | 40+ lines |
| New concepts | ≤ 3 per turn* | 4 (if related) | 5+ unprompted |
| Code duplication | <3 occurrences | 3 occurrences | 4+ occurrences |
| if/else branches | ≤ 3 branches | 3-4 branches | 5+ branches |

*Exception: When user explicitly requests specific number (e.g., "split into 5 classes")

---

## Enforcement Priority

1. **🔴 Blocking Issues** (MUST fix before proceeding)
   - Modified code outside user-specified scope
   - File >250 lines
   - Method >5 parameters
   - Violated SOLID principles

2. **🟡 Warning Issues** (SHOULD address)
   - File 200-250 lines
   - Method 4 parameters
   - Method >25 lines

3. **🟢 Advisory Issues** (Consider improving)
   - File 150-200 lines
   - Opportunities for design patterns
